  },
  "limitations": [
    "Python producer and complete Rust I/O/copy loop are not Verus-proved; actual span arithmetic is. Finite models are not a refinement of complete adapters.",
    "4 MiB is a producer policy, not an environment response/atomicity/latency guarantee. Legacy or external descriptors retain their encoded sizes.",
    "Per-attempt payload authentication bounds exclude metadata reads/allocations, retry multipliers and physical backend I/O. Growing metadata has memory/CPU costs and changes publication identities across producer policies.",
    "100 GB uses a native streaming source, not a 100 GB Python tensor allocation; separate 2 GiB + 17-byte installed-wheel runs cross the actual Python 512-digest threshold.",
    "Position-dependent native data and complete returned-byte oracle; Python independently checks full final-smoke chunk hashes and request prefixes/suffixes. Repeating Python probe data is compatibility evidence, not physical bandwidth evidence.",
    "No new physical TB evidence or filesystem bandwidth SLA. Publication excludes separately timed checksum preparation but includes stream regeneration, hashing, framing and sync.",
    "Cache state and background workload are uncontrolled; full formal/integration checks overlap on the writer host. Native-call timings exclude the following content oracle; workflow timings include SSH/oracle/small requests.",
    "GC is normal namespace reclamation after all readers exit, not measurement of backend object deletion. Private metadata and uploaded binaries are removed only after successful GC.",
    "The cost regression is reproduced; no claim that straw has no remaining bugs or proof gaps."
  ],
